From: Nuxel <nuxel@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ssp-native: nuxel_bbd_flash RX node + ROM-phase ownership fix

The boot-ROM GetVersion/MemoryWrite replies are raw SSI/TL bytes delivered on
/dev/ttyBCM (bcm_gps_spi.c bcm_on_packet_received -> priv->read_buf circ-buffer,
the non-peer branch).  nuxel_bbd_flash.c was reading them from /dev/bbd_sensor,
which under the native peer path (bbd_nuxel_peer_active) carries the SSP
application [u16 len][ssp_msg] frames from callback_bbd_on_packet, NOT the raw
boot-ROM TL stream.  Hence every ROM reply was silently dropped and rx=0.

Fix: during the ROM phase, read replies from /dev/ttyBCM (fd_tty), and do NOT
open/hold /dev/bbd_sensor as a peer in that phase, so the kernel keeps the raw
SSI RX path.  Keep /dev/bbd_control writes unchanged (gated, reversible).

This is a userspace correction; no kernel image change and no BOOT flash.
---
 tools/s10plus/ssp-native/nuxel_bbd_flash.c | 31 +++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/s10plus/ssp-native/nuxel_bbd_flash.c b/tools/s10plus/ssp-native/nuxel_bbd_flash.c
--- a/tools/s10plus/ssp-native/nuxel_bbd_flash.c
+++ b/tools/s10plus/ssp-native/nuxel_bbd_flash.c
@@
-    sess.fd_sensor = open(BBD_SENSOR, O_RDWR | O_NONBLOCK);
-    if (sess.fd_sensor < 0) {
-        logx("open %s: %s", BBD_SENSOR, strerror(errno));
-        ret = EXIT_TRANSPORT_UNAVAIL; goto out;
-    }
+    /*
+     * ROM-phase ownership: boot-ROM SSI/TL replies are raw RX bytes on
+     * /dev/ttyBCM.  Do NOT open /dev/bbd_sensor here: holding the native peer
+     * routes bcm_on_packet_received into the SSP app state machine instead of
+     * the raw SSI circ-buffer, which would swallow every ROM reply (rx=0).
+     */
+    sess.fd_sensor = -1;
@@
 static int pump(struct session *s, int ms)
 {
@@
-        struct pollfd p = { .fd = s->fd_sensor, .events = POLLIN };
+        struct pollfd p = { .fd = s->fd_tty, .events = POLLIN };
         int pr = poll(&p, 1, 50);
         if (pr <= 0) continue;
-        ssize_t r = read(s->fd_sensor, buf, sizeof buf);
+        ssize_t r = read(s->fd_tty, buf, sizeof buf);
         if (r < 0) {
             if (errno == EINTR || errno == EAGAIN) continue;
             break;
@@
-        rx_feed(&s->rx, buf, (size_t)r, on_pkt, s);
+        rx_feed(&s->rx, buf, (size_t)r, on_pkt, s);
---
